Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: translate per-experience hero titles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

experience_hero_titles (the random tagline shown at the very top of
the proposal page, e.g. "Luxury Under Sail") had no translation table
at all — getFullExperiences() read the raw English rows straight
through with no locale overlay, unlike title/short_description/
description/sections/facts, which already had one each.

- New migration: experience_hero_titles_translations, same shape as
  the other *_translations tables.
- syncHeroTitlesBatch() in translateExperience.ts, same one-Lara-call-
  per-experience batching as sections/facts, now called from
  syncFullExperienceTranslations() so hero titles translate at the
  same time as the rest of an experience's content when a proposal
  selects it.
- getFullExperiences() now fetches experience_hero_titles_translations
  and localizes each hero title through getLocalizedExperience(), the
  same helper already used for facts/sections/content.

